    "canvas": {
      "state": "present",
      "evidence": "CORE-05 (2026-11-23): the editor draws its preview on a canvas (src/editor/shell/Preview.tsx), in a box that is an image named \"Route animation preview\" (1.1.1, the reviewed snapshot); nothing in it could be operated until CORE-06. CORE-06 (2026-11-25, brief 112): the box is a toolbar with one tab stop (an application since brief 114, D245), and its canvas takes the pointer: the pen's tap places a point on the up-event, joined from the selected one, and Escape clears the selection; pointer-cancellation reads it while a press is held, after a press moved off and after a whole press (2.5.2). CORE-06 (2026-11-26, brief 116): a point on it is dragged by the pointer; point-drag-moves reads the dragged point's marker at its new place, not at its tap, after the release, and at its tap again, not at the new place, after one Undo, and point-drag-escape reads the whole canvas as before the press after Escape mid-drag and after the release that follows (2.5.2). The point's drag has no single-pointer alternative yet (2.5.7 owed, D250). CORE-06 (2026-11-26, brief 117, D252): in pen-drawn only, the preview's set-aside carries a measure (tests/a11y/project.mjs, PEN_DRAWN_ASIDE; run by contrastRows in tests/a11y/helpers.ts after the state's other contrast readings): skipped to the route's end, the line, both points' markers and the selected point's ring, each pixel composited over the box's own background and its ratio taken against it, each at 3:1 or it fails 1.4.11, as does a measure that reads nothing. It claims only the plain background with no picture in pen-drawn at the default settings; the user's own picture and routes in their own colours stay set aside (1.4.11, essential), and the other states that show the preview keep the set-aside unmeasured. No row of the catalogue is triggered by this feature alone."
    },
